   "rc": 0,
   "ruling": "Every proof search agrees. The difference is three trailing `true` lines: `!(bind! &kb (new-space))` answers True here and nothing upstream, whose bind! has one clause, `'bind!'(A, ['new-state', B], C) :- 'change-state!'(A, B, C)`, so binding anything else silently fails there and the name works afterwards only because a bare symbol already names a space. This engine binds any value to a token; that is a case upstream has no clause for rather than one it answers differently.",
